{"causes": ["The establishment of the Síl nÁedo Sláine dynasty by his grandfather Áed Sláine provided the necessary lineage for Sechnassach's claim to power.", "His father Blathmac mac Áedo Sláine and uncle Diarmait mac Áedo Sláine held the high kingship consecutively, consolidating the family's authority.", "The inherent system of dynastic succession within the Uí Néill confederation facilitated Sechnassach's ascent to the high kingship in 665 CE."], "effects": ["Sechnassach's reign continued the dynastic succession of the Síl nÁedo Sláine, reinforcing their claim to the High Kingship of Ireland.", "His death in 671 CE led to the succession of his brother Cenn Fáelad mac Blathmaic, maintaining the family's control over the Uí Néill.", "The lack of major recorded conflicts during his rule suggests a period of relative stability, contributing to the long-term consolidation of Uí Néill power."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "blathmac-mac-aedo-slaine", "sourceName": "Blathmac mac Áedo Sláine", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "sechnassach", "targetName": "Sechnassach", "context": "Sechnassach succeeded his father, Blathmac mac Áedo Sláine, as High King of Ireland in 665 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "sechnassach", "sourceName": "Sechnassach", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "early-medieval-ireland", "targetName": "Early Medieval Ireland", "context": "Sechnassach's rule as High King occurred during the politically complex Early Medieval period of Irish history."}, {"sourceSlug": "sil-naedo-slaine", "sourceName": "Síl nÁedo Sláine", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "sechnassach", "targetName": "Sechnassach", "context": "Sechnassach was a member of the Síl nÁedo Sláine, a powerful kindred of the southern Uí Néill."}, {"sourceSlug": "sechnassach", "sourceName": "Sechnassach", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "brega", "targetName": "Brega, Ireland", "context": "Sechnassach was King of Brega, a territory central to the Síl nÁedo Sláine's power, during his reign as Hig